Portions of the ext2/3/4 filesystem driver (sys/fs/ext2/) are derived
from FreeBSD's sys/fs/ext2fs/ codebase — specifically:

  - sys/fs/ext2/ext2_hash.c (htree name-hash functions: legacy,
    half-MD4, TEA) is a near-verbatim port of FreeBSD's
    sys/fs/ext2fs/ext2_hash.c.
  - The htree directory-index lookup in sys/fs/ext2/ext2.c follows
    FreeBSD's sys/fs/ext2fs/ext2_htree.c.
  - The per-superblock / per-bg-descriptor / per-inode metadata_csum
    algorithms in sys/fs/ext2/ext2.c follow FreeBSD's
    sys/fs/ext2fs/ext2_csum.c.
  - The xattr on-disk layout and walker in sys/fs/ext2/ext2_xattr.c
    follow FreeBSD's sys/fs/ext2fs/ext2_extattr.c.
  - The ext4 extent-tree resolver and append-write path in
    sys/fs/ext2/ext2.c reference FreeBSD's sys/fs/ext2fs/ext2_extents.c.

